Barley – agronomy topics
The decision whether to grow barley for the malting or feed grade depends on four main factors:
the premium paid for malt barley;
the relative yields of malting and feed grade barley;
agronomic and disease constraints of the different varieties; and
the likelihood that grain of a malting barley variety will be acceptable for inclusion into the malting grade.

