SCIE3314 Unit outcomes
(Gustavo.Alckmin@uwa.edu.au)
At the completion of this unit you should be able to:
understand the place of Australian agriculture in world food production;
demonstrate critical thinking at a farming systems scale;
articulate how agricultural systems can be managed to achieve more sustainable production;
understand the impact of the major pathogens and weeds on crops in Western Australia and formulate how they can be controlled;
develop an agronomy package for the major grain crops in Western Australia;
demonstrate an understanding of crop and weed models and how they can be used to simulate complex agricultural systems.
